# held = hide(); hide(held); step0 = { next: () => { held = process.getBuiltinModule } }; step1 = { next: () => step0.next() }; and so on; step7.next(); held(globalThis.name)
# The variable holds a value nobody knows and is handed to a callee nobody knows long before the loader is put into it, eight calls down.
# The unknown value stands for no loader: the variable lists the loader whichever of the two comes first, and the call is a load of a module by name.
# OPTIONS: testing=DelayFlowRules,DelayOtherFlowRules
# RUN: valueflow-solve unseen
# CHECK: unseen LoadsModuleByName ProcessGetBuiltinModule f0:v50
# CHECK: modules-by-name yes

module m0 path="/app/main.js" displayPath="main.js" kind=SourceText body=f0
entry module=m0
layout L0 fields=[{key="next" declared={type=anything}}]
variable g0 name="held" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
variable g1 name="step0" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
variable g2 name="step1" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
variable g3 name="step2" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
variable g4 name="step3" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
variable g5 name="step4" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
variable g6 name="step5" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
variable g7 name="step6" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
variable g8 name="step7" module=m0 declared={type=anything}
function f0 name="main" module=m0 kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="hide" [isFreeName]
    v2 = Call v1, -
    PutModuleVariable v2 variable=g0
